From e2de5c657511ba182c89f26f2f34ae54ab524096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lavavex <27239435+lavavex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:49:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/24] Home-screen tiles: start a game straight from its own
 tile

A tile is a tiny title of its own (title id, name, icon) built by
tools/build_tile.sh from native/tile/pw_tile_main.c. It reads the game
from its tile.conf and starts prospero-win with sceLncUtilLaunchApp and
"profile=<id> home=1", logging each launch attempt to
/data/prospero-win/logs/tile-<id>.log. prospero-win keeps doing the /data
elevation (the Lapy helper only serves PPSA99995), so tiles need none and
are a few hundred KB.

The title learns home=1: when the game ends it closes to Home instead of
restarting into the launcher.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
